    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the established idiom of this `Owner` model, which is already the hub for a large family of derived, read-only getters.\n\n- **Right unit / natural for a maintainer.** `getRiskFlag()` is a derived getter that composes other derived/stored attributes (`possibleDuplicate`, `capacityWarning`, email check) \u2014 exactly the shape of the existing `getOwnerSegment()`, `getMembershipLevel()`, `getContactPreference()`, `getTimezone()`, etc. A maintainer would expect this computed boolean to live right here alongside them.\n- **Helper decomposition matches local convention.** `isDisposableAdjacentEmail()` as a private instance helper mirrors `deriveRegion()`/`regionFromPostcode()`, and `secondLevelLabel()` as a private static string helper mirrors `leadingRegion()`, `extractCountryCode()`, `fiscalYearOf()`, and `luhnCheckDigit()`. The file consistently does inline string parsing with small private statics rather than reaching for util classes.\n- **Constant placement is consistent.** `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` as a `static final Set.of(...)` lookup table sits naturally with `CITY_REGION`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `COUNTRY_NATIONAL_LENGTH`, and `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS`.\n- **No duplication.** Domain parsing isn't repeated elsewhere; `getIdentityKey()` only lowercases the whole email and doesn't split the domain, so there's no overlapping logic to consolidate.\n- **Additive.** Nothing existing is restructured; the OpenAPI schema addition is placed next to the other derived read-only properties.\n\nNothing here makes `Owner` more of a catch-all than the codebase's existing design already is \u2014 the addition stays within that design rather than stretching it.",
